cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Agent OS: A Local-First Broker for Vendor-Neutral AI Agent Coordination"
message: "If you use Agent OS in research or industry work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Islam Santo"
    given-names: "Shifat"
    alias: "oneKn8"
    email: "shifatislamsanto764@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/oneKn8/agent-os"
url: "https://github.com/oneKn8/agent-os"
abstract: >
  Agent OS is a local-first operating system for AI agents that brokers
  across local, cloud-rented, and vendor-hosted agents (Claude Code,
  Codex CLI, Devin, ChatGPT/Operator, Cursor, custom GPTs, local LLMs).
  It exposes a normalized adapter layer over heterogeneous vendor APIs
  and provides supervisor-driven goal decomposition, cost-aware routing,
  typed inter-agent messaging, conflict arbitration, audit, and per-agent
  permission gates. The architecture is structurally defensible because
  no single vendor can ship a neutral broker (lock-in is every vendor's
  business model), and a cloud broker would itself become a vendor garden;
  local-first is the only natural home.
keywords:
